# Custom DNS records for the simulated internet, one "IP name..." per line as
# in /etc/hosts. Append lines, then restart the simulation or run
#   greybox-ctl exec topgen.info topgen-boot reload-dns
# e.g.
#   echo "12.0.0.50 intranet.example.com" >> /etc/topgen/hosts.custom
#
# - Any top level domain works, made-up ones included; every address also gets
#   a PTR record. A and PTR records only.
# - Records are added to the built-in ones and never replace them: a name that
#   the scraped sites, mail servers or backbone already define, or that appears
#   earlier in this file, is skipped with a warning, and so is a malformed line.
# - Only DNS changes: the machine at the address must exist on its own, e.g. a
#   VM on the external 12.0.0.0/24 network.
#
#12.0.0.50    intranet.example.com example.com
#12.0.0.52    portal.range.lab
